WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.459
You mentioned the middle class just now

00:00:02.459 --> 00:00:04.107
. Of course, some middle-class

00:00:04.107 --> 00:00:06.107
individuals may have different thoughts

00:00:06.107 --> 00:00:07.800
, feeling that while your social

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.543
welfare efforts are indeed great,

00:00:09.543 --> 00:00:11.595
we’ve seen universal cash handouts in

00:00:11.595 --> 00:00:12.362
recent years.

00:00:12.362 --> 00:00:14.254
>> Regarding these universal cash handouts

00:00:14.254 --> 00:00:16.146
, many in the middle class might wonder

00:00:16.146 --> 00:00:17.941
: why aren't these returned based on

00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:20.003
the amount of taxes paid? Some might

00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:22.728
think, "I have children to raise, taxes

00:00:22.728 --> 00:00:25.486
to pay, plus car loans and a mortgage."

00:00:25.486 --> 00:00:27.984
AI giants receive so many tax subsidies

00:00:27.984 --> 00:00:30.034
, and low-income groups receive

00:00:30.034 --> 00:00:32.276
corresponding social benefits, yet

00:00:32.276 --> 00:00:34.775
I’m the one paying most of the heavy

00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:37.209
taxes, and then you take my money for

00:00:37.209 --> 00:00:39.803
universal cash handouts. Does this make

00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:42.163
the middle class the victims in this

00:00:42.163 --> 00:00:44.633
K-shaped economic welfare policy? How

00:00:44.633 --> 00:00:46.257
do you view this issue?

00:00:46.257 --> 00:00:48.060
>> Here is the situation: as we just

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.023
discussed, actually 50%of our income

00:00:50.023 --> 00:00:52.033
tax comes from the top 1%of earners.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.001
>> Mm-hmm.

00:00:53.001 --> 00:00:54.451
>> That’s who pays it.

00:00:54.451 --> 00:00:57.328
>> Mm-hmm. If we were to distribute the AI

00:00:57.328 --> 00:00:59.492
dividend proportionally based on how

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.874
much tax people pay, then that would...

00:01:01.874 --> 00:01:03.896
>> End up going to corporations.

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.891
>> Right, they would just take it back.

00:01:05.891 --> 00:01:08.097
Secondly, we must acknowledge that

00:01:08.097 --> 00:01:10.467
everyone contributes to the economy.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.539
>> It shouldn't necessarily be evaluated

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.702
based on the amount of tax paid. Take

00:01:14.702 --> 00:01:16.460
taxi drivers, for example.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.831
>> They also contribute a great deal to

00:01:18.831 --> 00:01:19.380
Taiwan.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.940
>> Or a cleaning staff member. They keep a

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.120
company or a hospital running smoothly,

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.183
which is a significant contribution.

00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:28.193
Therefore, when we distribute this AI

00:01:28.193 --> 00:01:30.256
dividend, it should be on a per-person

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.372
basis, and it is not appropriate to use

00:01:32.372 --> 00:01:34.435
income level or tax amount as a metric

00:01:34.435 --> 00:01:37.530
for the whole picture. Yes, exactly.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.620
And especially for the middle class you

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.710
mentioned, we have other social welfare

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.535
systems in place to support them.

00:01:43.535 --> 00:01:45.258
>> For example, the "0 to 6 years old,

00:01:45.258 --> 00:01:46.790
raised by the state" program we

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:47.369
mentioned.

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:48.902
>> Or the 0 to 18-year-old growth

00:01:48.902 --> 00:01:50.830
allowance, free tuition for public and

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.809
private high schools, tuition subsidies

00:01:52.809 --> 00:01:54.342
for private colleges, and even

00:01:54.342 --> 00:01:56.435
long-term care 2.0. These are actually

00:01:56.435 --> 00:01:58.098
a huge help for the "sandwich

00:01:58.098 --> 00:01:59.362
generation" families.

00:01:59.362 --> 00:02:01.623
>> For those "sandwich" families who have

00:02:01.623 --> 00:02:03.827
parents to support above and children

00:02:03.827 --> 00:02:07.827
to raise below, this is a great help.
